mean60\"","\"median60\"","\"spread\"","\"zero_trade_days\"","\"reference_position_rupees\"","\"participations\"","\"L\"","\"not_zero\"","\"821.85\"","\"28200\"","\"market_secondary\"","\"market_crosscheck\"","\"HTTP403 for bhavcopy CSV,ZIP and ComHeader; no exchange bar retained\"","null","\"500000\"","\"0.02\"","\"0.05\"","\"0.10\"","\"Missing official BSE rows are ND, not zero. NSE absence is not BSE no trading. Price/volume are secondary crosschecked only.\"","\"BQS\"","\"GQS\"","\"IAS\"","\"terms\"","\"known_contribution\"","\"missing_weight\"","\"coverage\"","\"raw\"","\"cap\"","\"final\"","\"display\"","\"raw_bounds\"","\"effective_bounds\"","\"rank_eligible\"","\"factor\"","\"weight\"","\"score\"","\"contribution\"","\"GOV\"","\"0.20\"","5","\"1.00\"","\"MOAT\"","6","\"1.20\"","\"REV\"","\"0.12\"","8","\"0.96\"","\"DUR\"","7","\"0.70\"","\"CAP\"","\"0.84\"","\"CASH\"","3","\"0.30\"","\"BAL\"","\"0.08\"","\"0.40\"","\"EXEC\"","\"0.48\"","\"5.88\"","\"5.9\"","false","\"3.20\"","\"1.40\"","\"EARN\"","\"0.15\"","\"1.05\"","\"7.00\"","\"5.0\"","\"0.25\"","\"1.4700\"","\"R\"","\"0.35\"","\"D\"","\"0.60\"","\"P\"","\"2.0700\"","\"0.55\"","\"0.45\"","\"NS\"","\"2.6200\"","\"7.5700\"","\"shift\"","\"changed_score\"","\"gates_not_cured_by_score_changes\"","-1","\"0.80\"","\"5.68\"","\"5.7\"","\"1.4200\"","\"2.0200\"","\"2.5700\"","\"7.5200\"","true","1","\"6.08\"","\"6.1\"","\"1.5200\"","\"2.1200\"","\"2.6700\"","\"7.6200\"","\"5.76\"","\"5.8\"","\"2.80\"","\"6.60\"","\"1.4400\"","\"2.0400\"","\"2.5900\"","\"7.5400\"","9","\"1.08\"","\"6.00\"","\"6.0\"","\"3.60\"","\"7.40\"","\"1.5000\"","\"2.1000\"","\"2.6500\"","\"7.6000\"","\"5.78\"","\"6.80\"","\"1.4450\"","\"2.0450\"","\"2.5950\"","\"7.5450\"","\"5.98\"","\"1.60\"","\"7.20\"","\"1.4950\"","\"2.0950\"","\"2.6450\"","\"7.5950\"","\"0.72\"","\"0.90\"","\"6.85\"","\"7.15\"","2","\"6.90\"","\"7.10\"","\"7.1\"","\"0.32\"","\"5.80\"","\"1.4500\"","\"2.0500\"","\"2.6000\"","\"7.5500\"","\"5.96\"","\"1.4900\"","\"2.0900\"","\"2.6400\"","\"7.5900\"","\"0.56\"","\"1.8700\"","\"2.4200\"","\"7.3700\"","\"2.2700\"","\"2.8200\"","\"7.7700\"","\"facts\"","\"contrary\"","\"confidence\"","\"why\"","\"FY21–26 original audit and IFC opinions were unmodified; FY26 auditor change was mandatory rotation, not resignation.\"","\"FY26 sanctioned co-guarantees were ₹99.2185 crore and related purchases ₹76.3426 crore; CRISIL records India Ratings non-cooperation in 2021.\"","\"Related loans declined, and no substantiated diversion was found. Loan-term wording conflicts and changed IPO deployment still require explanation.\"","\"ar2021\"","\"ar2022\"","\"ar2023\"","\"ar2024\"","\"ar2025\"","\"ar2026\"","\"rating2026\"","\"Medium\"","\"Adequate disclosure but material connected exposures and changed capital allocation; not an evidenced severe governance failure.\"","\"Long execution history, qualifications and Gujarat utility relationships support access to T&D tenders.\"","\"Management reported 1,300 km of cable and 4,000 RMUs delivered in FY26, with escalation provisions in contracts.\"","\"Tender competition remains; two customers were 56.10% of sales and Gujarat 93% of June backlog. No demonstrated monopoly pricing.\"","\"transcript2026\"","\"Useful qualification/relationships, contestable against diversified EPC peers.\"","\"schedule\"","\"FY21–26 economically comparable EPC revenue rose from ₹111.60 crore to ₹1,627.94 crore; the pre-pandemic FY20 comparison is also strong.\"","\"FY26 restated-basis growth was 51.85%; H2 FY26 versus H2 FY25 was approximately 30.45%.\"","\"The FY21 trough and FY25 step-up inflate headline CAGR. Input-price pass-through and precise constant-price organic growth are not quantified.\"","\"prospectus\"","\"presentation2026\"","\"Starting score 9 for at least 30% CAGR; net adjustment 0; Medium-confidence comparability ceiling 8. Pandemic distortion is not penalized twice.\"","\"Economically consistent EPC revenue basis excluding JV turnover, with physical-delivery crosscheck. Not a claim of pure-volume CAGR.\"","\"March 2026 remaining performance obligations were ₹3,326 crore, recognized over one to five years.\"","\"June unexecuted orders of ₹3,164 crore and grid reinforcement demand provide an accessible medium-term tender runway.\"","\"Six customers represent 90% of backlog, concentrated in Gujarat. Pipeline is not won cash; BESS economics and finance remain conditional.\"","\"Strong accessible medium-term runway, not assured decade-long growth.\"","\"The funded-capital bridge includes receivables, retentions, guarantee deposits and fixed assets, not just PPE.\"","\"FY25–26 incremental normalized NOPAT / added capital is approximately 25.36%, above the 12–18% analytical discount range.\"","\"Only two aligned Ind AS years support the strongest calculation. Accrued profit needs collection, book PPE is low, longer-window bases are not comparable and BESS returns are unproven.\"","\"Historical accrued incremental economics are strong, but cash collection, basis limits and BESS qualifications prevent an exceptional score.\"","\"Comparable FY25–26 CFO totals −₹68.1223 crore against ₹239.8316 crore PAT.\"","\"FY24 CFO is negative across presentations; FY26 retention is ₹279.4349 crore and current AR ₹348.7721 crore, while deposits absorbed further cash.\"","\"Some earlier restated years show positive CFO and expansion absorbs capital. Repeated recent negative cash realization and supplier funding make this more than a single transient quarter.\"","\"High on FY25–26; Medium across classifications\"","\"Persistent weak realization supports CASH 3 and the GQS cap of 5.\"","\"Audited debt is ₹127.2338 crore against equity ₹406.1678 crore; operating EBIT covers reported interest about 18 times.\"","\"Only ₹1.3452 crore is unrestricted CCE; ₹79.9632 crore deposits are restricted and guarantee exposures are material.\"","\"CRISIL A-/Positive and moderate trailing utilization suggest flexibility, but rated lines are not unconditional available cash and the rating assumes no large debt-funded capex.\"","\"Reported leverage is manageable but liquidity, collateral and renewal remain sensitive.\"","\"FY25–26 EPC revenue and management-reported physical deliveries grew substantially.\"","\"₹25.1093 crore of original equipment, solar and hydrogen IPO objects remained unspent at 8 August 2026, with redirection proposed to BESS.\"","\"Delivery in EPC is demonstrated; new owned-asset commissioning and the promised cash collection improvement are not yet demonstrated.\"","\"Strong EPC delivery offsets, but does not erase, deferred original IPO projects.\"","\"FY26 operating EBIT is ₹196.0215 crore after excluding other income and JV profit and adding back the identified ₹0.6392 crore exception.\"","\"Reported diluted EPS increased from ₹59.75 to ₹79.52; FY26 issued shares remained 18,007,392 after the IPO.\"","\"Deferred-tax credit of ₹6.4847 crore and JV profit of ₹5.6911 crore affect PAT. Input-method estimates, mix and historical other income limit pure recurring-earnings confidence.\"","\"Operating and per-share growth are meaningful, but not wholly cash backed or tax normalized.\"","\"The five-year monthly cash model suppresses returns after any opening, pre-entry, intraperiod or terminal funding breach.\"","\"Actual entry cash and committed BESS finance remain unverified; the quoted close is only secondary-corroborated.\"","\"A cash-surviving conditional model is useful, but cannot become a supported central investment-return score.\"","\"Low\"","\"NS, not assigned a neutral or punitive return score.\"","\"Joint collection, supplier-credit, margin and guarantee stress creates finite funding shortfalls.\"","\"Owned BESS, restricted margin deposits and connected guarantees can force adverse recapitalization before reported earnings collapse.\"","\"Moderate reported leverage, audited assets and established utility customers offer recovery support. Stress failure does not prove current default or zero recovery.\"","\"Material impairment/adverse recapitalization under credible stress; not an assumed zero recovery.\"","\"Reverse growth tests preserve every failed candidate and distinguish funding boundaries from valid return roots.\"","\"Price-implied growth depends on future collections, capital intensity and project funding that are not verified at entry.\"","\"Headline P/E appears modest, but cannot on its own resolve retained cash, new project capital or terminal funding requirements.\"","\"NS because no supported central funding/valuation expectations can be scored.\"","\"The official 19 October security master gives 100-share lots and 18,007,392 shares.\"","\"Official BSE 20/60-session trading data, spreads and current restrictions were not retrieved; one secondary 28,200-share print is insufficient.\"","\"Trading is quoted and no suspension is established. Missing BSE rows or NSE absence must not be interpreted as zero volume.\"","\"security\"","\"NS: unavailable trading history cannot establish executable capacity.\"","\"gate\"","\"status\"","\"reason\"","\"G1\"","\"Conditional\"","\"No substantiated severe governance breach; connected guarantees, loan wording and capital-allocation changes require scrutiny.\"","\"G2\"","\"Current Ind AS financial statements and audits usable. Old CFO classifications and minor reconciliation differences retained, not spliced.\"","\"G3\"","\"Hold\"","\"Current available cash, committed drawable limits, debt renewal and BESS financing not verified at entry. A cash-surviving analyst scenario is not proof of actual funding; stress breach is not evidence of actual default.\"","\"G4\"","\"Official BSE 20/60-session liquidity, spread and restriction state missing. NSE interoperability does not establish NSE listing or BSE no-trade days.\"","\"year\"","\"period_end\"","\"basis\"","\"revenue\"","\"other_income\"","\"pbt\"","\"pat\"","\"owner_pat\"","\"da\"","\"finance_cost\"","\"cfo\"","\"cash_capex\"","\"debt\"","\"cash\"","\"equity\"","\"rec